Subject: [PATCH] t2bce: refuse hibernation before touching queues without rebuild support

A hibernation whose registered clients cannot drop and rebuild their queues is
refused up front instead of after client teardown has begun.

Rebased for linux-t2 7.2.7 (t2bce 6780d522).  The original change ran HCD
removal before the client PM prepare so that command replies could still use
the system event queue.  Upstream's VHCI pm_prepare_no_state now resumes the
event queues before removing the HCD, and the reworked no-state fallback
reopens the transport first, so that ordering is provided upstream and is not
duplicated.  What remains here is the fail-early refusal: a hibernation whose
clients lack queue-rebuild callbacks is refused before any client or transport
state has been touched.

---
diff --git a/drivers/staging/t2bce/t2bce_core/t2bce_main.c b/drivers/staging/t2bce/t2bce_core/t2bce_main.c
--- a/drivers/staging/t2bce/t2bce_core/t2bce_main.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/t2bce/t2bce_core/t2bce_main.c
@@ -980,6 +980,12 @@
         goto out_unlock;
     }
     bce->no_state_queues_dropped = false;
+    if (force_no_state && !t2bce_core_clients_pm_can_rebuild_no_state(bce)) {
+        /* Refuse before any client or transport state has been touched. */
+        pr_err("t2bce_core: hibernation refused: a client cannot rebuild queues\n");
+        status = -EOPNOTSUPP;
+        goto out_unlock;
+    }
 
     status = t2bce_core_clients_pm_prepare(bce);
     if (status) {
